.TH CYBAR 1 "2026-10-03" "Cybar 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cybar \- an X11 status bar configured in Lua
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cybar
.RI [ --config " path"]
.br
.B cybar
.RI [ --config " path"] " check"
.br
.B cybar
.RI [ --timeout " ms"] " {reload|quit|toggle [target]}"
.br
.B cybar
.RI [ --timeout " ms"] " {msg|request} module text..."
.br
.B cybar completions
.I shell
.SH DESCRIPTION
Cybar creates status bars on a Linux X11 desktop. Configuration is a Lua file
returning a table of bars, themes, sections, and modules. LuaJIT is the default
build; Lua 5.4 is a mutually exclusive build option. Lua is bundled at build time.
Wayland is not supported.
.PP
Built-in modules show EWMH workspaces, the active window title, the clock, CPU
and RAM usage, and an XEMBED system tray. Custom sources poll Lua functions,
run commands asynchronously, or consume file/socket/command streams.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --config " path"
Read this configuration instead of the default. This applies to daemon startup
and check; control commands operate on the running display-specific instance.
.TP
.BI --timeout " ms"
Client request timeout in milliseconds. Default: 1000. Applicable to reload,
quit, toggle, and request. Message delivery is fire-and-forget.
The target-existence preflight for msg also uses this timeout.
.TP
.B --help
Display command help.
.TP
.B --version
Display the program version.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B check
Evaluate and validate configuration without opening X windows. Lua construction
code runs, so any direct Lua I/O in the file also runs.
.TP
.B reload
Reload configuration. On load, validation, or preparation failure, keep the
active bars and return the error to the client.
.TP
.B quit
Stop the daemon and release windows, reserved screen space, and the tray.
.TP
.B toggle [target]
Show or hide all bars, or the named bar/monitor. Hidden bars release their struts.
.TP
.B msg module text...
Check that the named module exists, then send text to its on_message handler
and exit after writing.
Callback errors are logged by the daemon, with no reply.
.TP
.B request module text...
Invoke on_message and print its return value. Exit nonzero on timeout or error.
.TP
.B completions shell
Print completions for bash, elvish, fish, powershell, or zsh.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGUSR1
Reload configuration.
.TP
.B SIGINT, SIGTERM
Shut down cleanly.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/cybar/config.lua
Default config when XDG_CONFIG_HOME is set.
.TP
.B ~/.config/cybar/config.lua
Default config otherwise.
.TP
.B $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/cybar/display-<hex-display>.sock
Private JSON Lines control socket. The containing directory has mode 0700;
the socket has mode 0600. If XDG_RUNTIME_DIR is unset, Cybar uses a private
/tmp/cybar-<uid> directory.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DISPLAY, XAUTHORITY
Select and authorize the X11 connection. DISPLAY also selects the control socket.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME, HOME
Locate configuration and expand tilde paths.
.TP
.B XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
Locate the private control socket.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero on success; nonzero on invalid startup configuration, missing instance,
unknown target, request timeout, or other errors. Fire-and-forget messages cannot
report daemon-side handler errors to their sender.
.SH NOTES
Module targets accept name@monitor to select a replicated module on one output.
An unqualified name selects the primary output's copy, or the first matching
instance.
.PP
All Lua callbacks run on the main thread and must return promptly. Use spawn,
exec, after, every, and socket helpers for asynchronous work. The watchdog logs
slow calls after they return; it cannot interrupt them.
.PP
Detached exec commands continue through configuration reload and daemon shutdown.
Captured spawn jobs and timers are retired with their configuration generation.
.PP
Configuration and required Lua files are watched with debounce when auto_reload
is enabled. Errors appear on daemon stderr, not in desktop notifications.
